  {
   "id": "svg-inline-icon",
   "why": "TOK-1's counterpart, and the exclusion people expect that is WRONG: <svg> is not excluded, its <text> renders visible words and is tokenized, and an inline svg must never cause its parent block to lose its OWN direct text. 8.0.1 states it behaviourally because the structural reading (“walk svg as a block”) regressed the commonest markup there is when PHP implemented it: every icon-bearing heading, link and list item lost its words. Token ORDER is part of the rule — the block's own text and the svg's text, in document order.",
